surya: battery SOC from the power-on OCV and a coulomb counter

Only when the locally built ADT has /surya-battery (capacity and the 25 C
OCV-by-SOC column of the surya battery profile): start SOC from the QG's
S7_PON_OCV (only if it agrees with V - I*R now) through that table, then
the battery current sampled every second
is integrated; publish and log every 30 s; SMB5 termination sets 100%; a
failed read keeps the last values instead of the 100% fallback. Without the
node SweetBattery is unchanged for sweet.

Read-only charger diagnostics: APSD type, ICL setting/status, AICL, FCC;
the PM6150 RTC seconds at start (needs 0902).

